\f0\fs22 \cf0 # Geographic Research: Sublime Point to Ruined Castle Gully (REVISED)\
\
## **1. Real-World Geographic Data**\
\
### **Sublime Point, Leura:**\
- **Elevation:** ~940 meters above sea level\
- **Location:** On the cliff edge of the Blue Mountains escarpment\
- **Features:** Lookout point with panoramic views over Jamison Valley\
- **Access:** Via Sublime Point Road from Leura\
\
### **Ruined Castle (Pulpit Rock area):**\
- **Elevation:** ~650-700 meters above sea level (the rock formation itself)\
- **Valley Floor Below:** ~300-350 meters above sea level\
- **Location:** Rock formation in the Jamison Valley, south of Katoomba/Leura\
- **Features:** Dramatic sandstone pillars, remote bushland location\
\
### **Distance & Terrain:**\
- **Direct Line Distance:** Approximately 3.5-4 kilometers\
- **Elevation Drop:** ~240-290 meters from Sublime Point to Ruined Castle formation\
- **Additional Drop to Valley Floor:** Another ~300-350 meters below the castle\
- **Terrain Between:** \
  - Sheer cliff faces (the escarpment wall)\
  - Dense eucalyptus forest\
  - Sandstone cliff systems\
  - Deep gullies and valleys\
  - No direct surface access\'97requires either:\
    - Steep bushwalking tracks (several hours)\
    - Cliff descent routes\
    - Or... a secret tunnel\
\
### **Geological Context:**\
- **Sandstone:** Hawkesbury sandstone formation (ideal for tunneling)\
- **Natural Caves:** The area contains natural cave systems and overhangs\
- **Cliff Structure:** Layered sedimentary rock with natural fault lines\
- **Water:** Underground water systems, seasonal creek flows\
