### **SECTION THREE: The Traverse Proper (The Horizontal Run)**\
\
#### **Transport System: "The Worm"**\
\
**Primary Transport:** Automated maglev pod system (on-demand dispatch)\
- **Track Length:** 3,847 meters (accounting for curve/descent)\
- **Pod Capacity:** 6 passengers + luggage OR cargo configuration (1,500kg)\
- **Speed:** 120 km/h\
- **Journey Time:** Approximately 2 minutes 15 seconds\
- **Sound:** Disturbingly quiet (magnetic levitation + sound dampening)\
- **Lighting:** Strips along tunnel walls create streaking effect\
- **Sensation:** Like being fired through a very expensive gun barrel\
\
**Dispatch Protocol:**\
- On-demand only\'97no scheduled service\
- Request via Junction Alpha control or Ruined Castle dispatch\
- Average wait time: 3-5 minutes (if pod must return from other end)\
- Priority override available (Eloise, emergency situations)\
- Maximum 4 pods can operate simultaneously (though rarely needed)\
\
**Pod Design:**\
- Aerodynamic capsule, 4m long\
- Wraparound windows (because apparently Eloise wants you to see exactly how much rock is above you)\
- Individual climate control\
- Emergency oxygen supply\
- Communication system with both junction points\
- Seats that are somehow both comfortable and remind you you're in a vehicle that could malfunction catastrophically\
\
**Track Construction:**\
- Magnetic rail system embedded in tunnel floor\
- Power supplied by redundant systems (grid power + backup generators + emergency power source that engineers won't discuss)\
- Automatic switching at Junction Alpha allows multiple pods to operate\
- Pod tracking system monitors all movements in real-time\
\
**The Tunnel Itself:**\
\
**Diameter:** 6 meters (allows pod clearance + maintenance access)\
\
**Construction Method:**\
- Primary boring through sandstone using tunnel boring machine (TBM)\
- Secondary shaping with precision cutting (method classified)\
- Reinforcement: Steel-reinforced concrete ribs every 3 meters\
- Waterproofing: Multi-layer membrane system\
- Drainage: Continuous channel along base (Blue Mountains gets wet)\
\
**Geological Integration:**\
Where possible, route follows natural fault lines and integrates existing cave systems. In three locations, tunnel opens into natural caverns:\
\
1. **The Cathedral** (1.2km from Sublime Point)\
   - Natural cavern, 15m high\
   - Tunnel passes through, creating surreal experience\
   - Stalactites preserved (Eloise's one concession to natural beauty)\
   - Emergency shelter designation Alpha-2\
\
2. **The Squeeze** (2.1km from Sublime Point)\
   - Narrow section where geology forced tunnel to minimum safe diameter\
   - Claustrophobic even by tunnel standards\
   - Pods slow to 60 km/h automatically\
   - Site of recurring anxiety dreams among staff\
\
3. **The Gallery** (3.4km from Sublime Point, approaching Ruined Castle)\
   - Large natural chamber converted to equipment storage\
   - Also serves as maintenance depot for pod system\
   - Contains spare pod, tools, emergency supplies\
   - Access: Side passage from main tunnel\
\
**Environmental Control:**\
- Positive air pressure throughout (prevents water ingress)\
- Air recycled every 12 minutes\
- Temperature/humidity monitored continuously\
- Atmospheric composition sensors (mining tunnels can accumulate gases)\
- Emergency protocols for fire, flood, collapse\
\
**Descent Profile:**\
The tunnel doesn't descend evenly. Gradient varies:\
- First kilometer: Gentle 5-degree slope\
- Middle section: Steeper 12-degree descent through escarpment\
- Final approach: Levels out, then slight rise to Ruined Castle facility\
\
**The Psychological Effect:**\
First-time passengers report sensation of "falling sideways." The combination of speed, descent, and enclosed space triggers primal responses. Eloise considers this "effective security screening"\'97anyone who can't handle the Traverse probably shouldn't be working with Gyges Discs.\
\
**Maintenance:**\
- Full structural inspection quarterly\
- Pod system serviced monthly\
- Drainage system checked weekly (water is the enemy)\
- Rock stability monitoring continuous\
- Emergency drills biannually\
\
**Communications:**\
- Fiber optic cables run length of tunnel\
- Redundant radio system (though rock interferes)\
- Emergency phones every 200 meters\
- Pod tracking system monitors all movements\
- Eloise can observe any transit in real-time (because of course she can)\
\
**Security:**\
- No external access points along entire length\
- Motion sensors detect any attempt to enter from cave systems\
- Pressure sensors detect structural changes\
- Cameras at intervals (infrared, low-light capable)\
- Automated lockdown if breach detected\
\
**The Cultural Element:**\
Staff call it "commuting through the earth's intestines." There's an unofficial tradition: First-timers must ride in silence. Veterans are allowed to chat, read, or (in one memorable case) play didgeridoo poorly.\
\
