\
**The Complete Underground Complex:**\
Entire facility is underground, carved into the sandstone cliff system. Nothing visible from surface\'97no buildings, no structures, no external indication of presence.\
\
**Surface Camouflage:**\
The Ruined Castle rock formation itself is untouched. Natural bushland maintained. From ground or air, the area appears completely undisturbed. Access points hidden in cliff faces, disguised as natural rock features or minor cave openings.\
\
**The Facility Layout:**\
- Central arrival hub (pod terminal)\
- Multiple levels radiating outward into cliff system\
- Primary Gyges research laboratories at deepest secure levels\
- Testing chambers purpose-built in newly excavated spaces (no natural cave systems compromised for testing\'97environmental integrity maintained)\
- Isolation: If something goes catastrophically wrong, valley location provides natural containment\
\
**Observation Deck:**\
- Located at facility's highest secure level\
- Looks out across Jamison Valley through narrow horizontal slot cut into cliff face\
- From outside: appears as natural shadow/crack in rock face\
- From inside: panoramic view across valley\
- Access restricted to senior staff\
- Staff joke it's where you go to contemplate career choices before returning to work that might kill everyone\
\
**The View:**\
The irony that the most beautiful view at Shakti Enterprises is at the most dangerous facility is not lost on anyone.\
