## **4. The Heavy Freight System: "The Burrow"**\
\
**Purpose:** Equipment too large/heavy for pods, bulk materials, emergency backup\
\
**Method:** \
- Dual-gauge automated rail system\
- Runs parallel to main tunnel (separate bore, 8m diameter)\
- Connected to maglev tunnel by cross-passages every 500m\
- Much slower than pod system but vastly higher capacity\
\
**The Rolling Stock:**\
\
**Locomotives:** Two automated electric units\
- Staff-named: **"Wombat"** and **"Echidna"**\
- Electric drive, powered by overhead catenary\
- Can be manually driven for precision work\
- Automated operation for standard runs\
- Speed: 40 km/h maximum (slower in automated mode)\
- Powerful enough to haul 50 tonnes\
\
**Rail Cars:**\
- Flatbed freight cars (modular, can be configured)\
- Enclosed cargo containers (for sensitive equipment)\
- Personnel carrier (converted mining car, holds 40 in emergency)\
- Specialized carriers for outsize equipment\
- Tank car (for transporting liquids, chemicals, or things staff don't ask about)\
\
**Operations:**\
- On-demand dispatch (like pod system)\
- Journey time: ~15 minutes Sublime Point to Ruined Castle\
- Typical usage: 2-3 freight runs per day\
- Heavy equipment moves (machinery, construction materials)\
- Bulk supplies for long-term facility operation\
- Emergency evacuation capability (can move entire staff if needed)\
\
**The Automation:**\
- Fully automated for standard cargo runs\
- Manual override available\
- Collision avoidance with pod system (separate tunnels, but interlocked control)\
- Real-time tracking from Junction Alpha control room\
\
