## **5. The Construction Story (Historical Background)**\
\
### **The Multi-Year Project: "The Dig"**\
\
**Phase 1: Planning & Deception**\
- Eloise acquires Sublime Point property through shell company\
- Simultaneously secures "geological research" rights for Ruined Castle area\
- Files permits for "advanced telecommunications infrastructure"\
- Strategic funding to environmental groups ensures conservation compliance\
- Hires mining consultants from multiple countries (none see full plan)\
\
**Phase 2: The Bore**\
- TBM deployed under cover of "infrastructure project"\
- Boring proceeds from both ends simultaneously\
- Spoil (excavated rock) distributed across multiple legitimate construction projects\
- Night work explained as "telecommunications infrastructure installation"\
- Environmental monitoring ensures no damage to natural cave systems\
\
**Phase 3: Reinforcement & Systems**\
- Concrete ribs installed\
- Maglev system built by company that "definitely doesn't exist"\
- Rail system added for heavy freight capacity\
- Water management systems critical (Blue Mountains = underground water)\
- Multiple near-discoveries by government inspectors, all resolved with strategic donations\
\
**Phase 4: Interior Fit-Out**\
- Pod system tested (first test: catastrophic failure, subsequent tests: improvements)\
- Stations completed\
- Communication systems activated\
- Security measures installed\
- Ruined Castle facility excavation completed (separate from tunnel construction)\
\
**Phase 5: Operational Testing & Concealment**\
- System run in "testing mode" for extended period\
- Staff relocated incrementally\
- Surface evidence at Ruined Castle eliminated\
- Official story solidified: "Private secure infrastructure for business operations"\
\
**Casualties:**\
- Zero deaths (remarkable for project of this scope)\
- Seventeen injuries (mostly minor)\
- One tunnel boring machine operator who "saw things he shouldn't" and now lives very comfortably abroad\
- Countless government regulations creatively interpreted\
- One geologist who tried to whistleblow (currently working on Aged Care documentation)\
\
